  "title": "Commit-message rules enforced on both the hook and the commit scan",
  "summary": "Adds two structural commit-message rules — the subject must exist and must not end in a full stop — and makes the four structural rules CONTRIBUTING.md states (those two plus bare-reference and reference-without-label) run on the commit scan as well as the commit-msg hook. A new COMMIT_GATE_RULES list and commit_gate_findings helper reuse the existing writing lint in commit context, so the pre-push checkpoint and the pull-request scan now fail a range whose messages break them, while the forge's generated merge subject stays exempt.",
